<title>GREECE: GREEK CITIBANK KEEPS BASE LOAN, DEPOSIT RATES UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>GREEK CITIBANK KEEPS BASE LOAN, DEPOSIT RATES UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will keep its lending</p>
<p>and deposit rates unchanged for a week effective Tuesday, it</p>
<p>said in a statement.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 17.00 percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 18.50 percent</p>
<p>** Special base rate for public enterprises and organisations</p>
<p>(DEKO) at 18.25 percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 18.50 percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 18 percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans at 24 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 23 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Rates on working capital loans denominated in foreign</p>
<p>currency for the coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  8.06 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.59 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  2.94 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.31 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.75 percent</p>
<p>    Pounds Sterling:  8.43 percent</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
